 then reassign.\nChanging the assignee alone leaves the routing wrong for next time."],[607,"**A complaint you expect is missing.** You only see complaints for the\nregions you are assigned to. If it belongs to a neighbouring district, it\nwill not appear for you."],[442,"**A region is missing.** Add it at the right level; do not attach it to the\nwrong parent as a shortcut, because visibility for every officer above it\nfollows that parent."],[440,"**A user sees nothing after signing in.** They have no region assignment.\nThis is the most common report by a wide margin."],[362,"**ACTIONS** — what you can do next."],[428,"**An account by itself grants nothing.** What determines which complaints a\nperson can see is the **region they are assigned to** — not their role. Staff\nin this system typically hold the same set of duties as each other and differ\nonly by region. A new user with no region assignment signs in successfully and\nsees an empty system."],[354,"**Assigned**"],[377,"**Average Resolution**"],[381,"**Category Trends** — Complaint, Service Issue, Question, Other."],[36,"**Category** — what your complaint is about:"],[387,"**Check for Updates** sends anything waiting and pulls down anything new.\nDo this whenever you get back into signal."],[550,"**Citizen Information may be empty, and that is deliberate.** People are\nallowed to report anonymously. An empty contact tab is not a data problem and\nis not something to chase — it means nobody may be called about this\ncomplaint, and the outcome has to be published through the tracking code\ninstead."],[87,"**Closed**"],[280,"**Collect Reports from Citizens**"],[39,"**Complaint**"],[441,"**Complaints reach the wrong office.** Check the region structure first and\nthe routing rules second — a misplaced region explains most of these."],[405,"**Default Language** here sets the labels that both citizens and staff see.\nChoose it deliberately: changing it later changes the interface for everyone\non the project at once."],[53,"**Description** — what happened, where, and how it affected you. At least\n10 characters, up to 5,000."],[363,"**DETAILS** — everything that was recorded about it."],[305,"**Do not receive updates**"],[388,"**Download all my data again** rebuilds the phone's copy from scratch. Use\nit only if complaints or projects you expect are missing."],[18,"**English**"],[386,"**Everything synchronized** with a green dot, and the time of the last\nsync, means the phone and the server agree."],[315,"**Filing on behalf of someone else** — an individual, or an organisation."],[19,"**Français**"],[324,"**Get GPS Location** — use this when you are standing at the spot."],[364,"**HISTORY** — every step anyone has taken on it, with names and dates."],[319,"**How it reached you** — In Person, Phone Call, SMS, Email, Verbal or\nWritten. Choose the channel the person actually used, not the device you\nare typing on."],[465,"**How it reached you** — In Person, Phone Call, SMS, Email, Verbal, Written"],[59,"**I want updates**"],[488,"**Ibibazo Bifunguye** (*Open Issues*) in the sidebar lists complaints that are\nstill active."],[560,"**Igenzura → Ibyitwajwe** (*Supervision → Escalated*) — complaints raised to\na higher level, usually because they passed their time limit or needed\nauthority the assigned officer did not have."],[561,"**Igitekerezo → Ubujurire** (*Feedback → Appeals*) — where someone has come\nback dissatisfied with the outcome."],[83,"**In Progress**"],[554,"**Is the category right?** A \"Question\" misfiled as a \"Complaint\" enters a\nresolution process it never needed."],[553,"**Is the region right?** Routing follows the region on the complaint. If it\nis wrong, the complaint sits with an office that cannot act on it."],[47,"**Issue Type** — how you are reporting it. Choosing from the website, pick\n**Web Form**. The other options (In Person, Phone Call, SMS, Email, Verbal,\nWritten, Mobile App) are used by officers recording a complaint on someone\nelse's behalf."],[478,"**Issue Type** records the channel the complaint arrived through, not how\nserious it is. If someone telephoned you, choose **Phone Call** — not\n**Web Form**, even though you are typing it into a web page. These figures are\nused to decide which channels the public actually rely on."],[314,"**Keep name confidential** — the name is stored but only the officer\nresolving the complaint can see it."],[17,"**Kinyarwanda** (the default)"],[81,"**New**"],[48,"**Next** stays grey until you have picked one of each."],[566,"**Nobody is available in the assigned department.** Reassign to another\nofficer rather than leaving it unassigned — an unassigned complaint has no\nowner and will not be picked up by anyone."],[352,"**Open**"],[45,"**Other**"],[43,"**Question**"],[309,"**Receive alerts directly**"],[307,"**Receive updates from facilitator**"],[269,"**Record a complaint** a citizen brings to you, through a six-step\nconversation designed to be read aloud."],[89,"**Rejected**"],[85,"**Resolved**"],[356,"**Resolved**"],[375,"**Resolved**"],[430,"**Routing** decides which department or role receives a complaint, based on\nits category and region."],[282,"**Search Reports**"],[270,"**See the complaints assigned to you**, and what stage each one is at."],[271,"**See the figures** for your area — how many complaints, how many resolved,\nhow long they take."],[41,"**Service Issue**"],[505,"**Someone reports the same problem twice.** Record it anyway and mention the\nearlier tracking code in the description. A reviewer will merge them."],[432,"**Statuses** are the stages a complaint passes through. Some are marked as\n*final*, meaning the complaint is finished."],[57,"**Stay anonymous**"],[61,"**Stay anonymous** is selected by default. Either way you still get a tracking\ncode, and you can still check the status yourself at any time."],[12,"**Submit a Complaint → Start form**"],[284,"**Sync Files**"],[325,"**Tap on the map** — use this when the person is describing somewhere else.\nTap, and drag the pin to adjust."],[593,"**The cards in the middle** group everything else by the kind of work it\nbelongs to — intake, feedback, supervision, projects, users, and system\nsettings. You will only be able to open the ones your role allows."],[318,"**The date** — when the problem happened, not today. Tap **Set for Today**\nonly if it is happening now. Tick **Current event or multiple occurrences**\nfor something ongoing."],[321,"**The description** — in the person's own words, as fully as you can. A\nreviewer who was not there has only this to work from."],[66,"**The Next button stays grey.** A required field on that step is still\nempty. On step 1 you need both a category and an issue type; on step 3 the\ndescription must be at least 10 characters."],[503,"**The region you need is not in the list.** Choose the nearest level above\nit and name the exact place in the description. Then tell your administrator\nthe region is missing."],[567,"**The same problem is reported twice.** Resolve one and record the other's\ntracking code in the outcome, so both codes give the person a real answer."],[578,"**The sidebar on the left** is always there. Its entries are:"],[94,"**The status has not changed in a long time.** Contact the office handling\nthe project and quote your tracking code."],[373,"**This Week**"],[431,"**Time limits** set how long each stage may take before a complaint escalates\non its own."],[371,"**Total Issues**"],[14,"**Track a Complaint → Enter code**"],[382,"**Type Trends** — the channel complaints arrived through: Mobile App, In\nPerson, Email, Web Form, SMS, Phone Call."],[286,"**View Reports**"],[320,"**What kind of issue** — Complaint, Service Issue, Question or Other."],[486,"**What specifically went wrong**, in the person's own words rather than a\nsummary like \"service problem\"."],[339,"**What specifically went wrong**, in their words rather than a summary like\n\"service problem\"."],[52,"**When did this happen?** — the date of the problem. Today's date is filled\nin already; change it if the problem happened earlier."],[485,"**When exactly.** A date, even an approximate one."],[338,"**When exactly** — a date, even an approximate one."],[484,"**Where exactly.** A village or facility name, not just a district. This is\nwhat decides who receives it."],[337,"**Where exactly** — a village, facility or landmark, not just a district."],[487,"**Whether they want to be contacted.** If they do, take a phone number. If\nthey would rather not be named, that is their right — record it anonymously\nand say so."],[340,"**Whether they want to be contacted**, and a number if they do."],[68,"**You closed the page mid-way.** Nothing is saved until you press\n**Submit Complaint**, so start again from the beginning."],[93,"**You lost the code.** If you gave contact details when you submitted, the\noffice can look your complaint up for you. If you chose to stay anonymous,\nthere is no way to recover it — you would need to submit again."],[504,"**You saved it with the wrong details.** Open the complaint and use\n**Reassign Issue** for the wrong owner, or ask a reviewer for anything else\n— once submitted, some fields are locked to keep the record trustworthy."],[606,"**You sign in but see almost nothing.** You have an account but no region\nassignment yet. Until an administrator assigns you to a region, there are no\ncomplaints you are allowed to see."],[67,"**Your location is not in the list.** Choose the closest area above it and\nname the exact place in the description instead."],[605,"**Your password does not work.** Passwords are not shown to anyone, so a\nreset is the only fix — ask your administrator."],[24,"<Card title=\"Check a complaint\" description=\"Use your tracking code to see the current status.\" href=\"/docs/citizen/track\" />"],[251,"<Card title=\"I assign and resolve complaints\" description=\"Reviewer or Supervisor — check new complaints, send them to the right officer, and